2025-05-01 02:20:08 - Thread-794 (execute) - INFO - [Exploration]
Relevant columns, their potential usage, and typical conditions  
• `pitcherId`: unique identifier of the pitcher – used to group, join, and filter rows that belong to the same pitcher.  
• `pitcherFirstName`, `pitcherLastName`: build the pitcher’s full name for display.  
• `pitchSpeed`: numeric value whose (non‑zero) maximum we want to keep.  Condition: `pitchSpeed > 0`.  
• `homeTeamId`, `homeTeamName`, `awayTeamId`, `awayTeamName`: identify the team for which the pitcher was playing in that particular game.  
• `homeFielder1 … homeFielder12`, `homeBatter1 … homeBatter9`, `awayFielder1 … awayFielder12`, `awayBatter1 … awayBatter9`: the roster snapshots that allow us to confirm a given `pitcherId` really appeared for either the home or the away team.  Condition example:  
  – `pitcherId IN UNNEST([homeFielder1 , … , homeBatter9])` → pitcher was on the home team.  
  – `pitcherId IN UNNEST([awayFielder1 , … , awayBatter9])` → pitcher was on the away team.  
• `seasonType` / table choice (`games_wide` for REG season, `games_post_wide` for PST) – both must be scanned (or unioned).  

Below are 10 exploratory / building‑block queries (each limited to 20 rows) that move from simple inspection toward the final answer.  
All tables live in the public project `bigquery-public-data.baseball`.

```sql
-- Description: 1) Quick look at several pitch speed values in regular‑season data
SELECT gameId, pitcherId, pitcherFirstName, pitcherLastName, pitchSpeed
FROM `bigquery-public-data.baseball.games_wide`
WHERE pitchSpeed IS NOT NULL
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- Description: 2) Make sure we only keep non‑zero pitch speeds
SELECT gameId, pitcherId, pitchSpeed
FROM `bigquery-public-data.baseball.games_wide`
WHERE pitchSpeed > 0
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- Description: 3) Same check for post‑season games
SELECT gameId, pitcherId, pitchSpeed
FROM `bigquery-public-data.baseball.games_post_wide`
WHERE pitchSpeed > 0
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- Description: 4) Distinct pitchers with at least one registered pitch speed (REG+PST)
SELECT DISTINCT pitcherId
FROM (
  SELECT pitcherId FROM `bigquery-public-data.baseball.games_wide`  WHERE pitchSpeed > 0
  UNION DISTINCT
  SELECT pitcherId FROM `bigquery-public-data.baseball.games_post_wide` WHERE pitchSpeed > 0
)
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- Description: 5) Sample rows where we verify the pitcher appears on the home roster
SELECT pitcherId, pitchSpeed, homeTeamId, homeTeamName
FROM `bigquery-public-data.baseball.games_wide`
WHERE pitchSpeed > 0
  AND pitcherId IN UNNEST([
        homeFielder1, homeFielder2, homeFielder3, homeFielder4, homeFielder5, homeFielder6,
        homeFielder7, homeFielder8, homeFielder9, homeFielder10, homeFielder11, homeFielder12,
        homeBatter1 , homeBatter2 , homeBatter3 , homeBatter4 , homeBatter5 ,
        homeBatter6 , homeBatter7 , homeBatter8 , homeBatter9
      ])
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- Description: 6) Sample rows where we verify the pitcher appears on the away roster
SELECT pitcherId, pitchSpeed, awayTeamId, awayTeamName
FROM `bigquery-public-data.baseball.games_post_wide`
WHERE pitchSpeed > 0
  AND pitcherId IN UNNEST([
        awayFielder1, awayFielder2, awayFielder3, awayFielder4, awayFielder5, awayFielder6,
        awayFielder7, awayFielder8, awayFielder9, awayFielder10, awayFielder11, awayFielder12,
        awayBatter1 , awayBatter2 , awayBatter3 , awayBatter4 , awayBatter5 ,
        awayBatter6 , awayBatter7 , awayBatter8 , awayBatter9
      ])
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- Description: 7) Build a view‑like UNION of regular & post‑season (only needed columns)
SELECT
  gameId,
  pitcherId,
  CONCAT(pitcherFirstName, ' ', pitcherLastName) AS pitcher_name,
  pitchSpeed,
  CASE
    WHEN pitcherId IN UNNEST([
          homeFielder1, homeFielder2, homeFielder3, homeFielder4, homeFielder5, homeFielder6,
          homeFielder7, homeFielder8, homeFielder9, homeFielder10, homeFielder11, homeFielder12,
          homeBatter1 , homeBatter2 , homeBatter3 , homeBatter4 , homeBatter5 ,
          homeBatter6 , homeBatter7 , homeBatter8 , homeBatter9
        ]) THEN homeTeamId
    WHEN pitcherId IN UNNEST([
          awayFielder1, awayFielder2, awayFielder3, awayFielder4, awayFielder5, awayFielder6,
          awayFielder7, awayFielder8, awayFielder9, awayFielder10, awayFielder11, awayFielder12,
          awayBatter1 , awayBatter2 , awayBatter3 , awayBatter4 , awayBatter5 ,
          awayBatter6 , awayBatter7 , awayBatter8 , awayBatter9
        ]) THEN awayTeamId
  END AS teamId
FROM (
  SELECT * FROM `bigquery-public-data.baseball.games_wide`
  UNION ALL
  SELECT * FROM `bigquery-public-data.baseball.games_post_wide`
)
WHERE pitchSpeed > 0
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- Description: 8) Compute each pitcher’s top pitch speed per team (REG+PST)
SELECT
  teamId,
  pitcherId,
  MAX(pitchSpeed) AS max_pitch_speed
FROM (
  /* Re‑use the roster‑check logic from the previous query */
  SELECT
    pitchSpeed,
    pitcherId,
    CASE
      WHEN pitcherId IN UNNEST([
            homeFielder1, homeFielder2, homeFielder3, homeFielder4, homeFielder5, homeFielder6,
            homeFielder7, homeFielder8, homeFielder9, homeFielder10, homeFielder11, homeFielder12,
            homeBatter1 , homeBatter2 , homeBatter3 , homeBatter4 , homeBatter5 ,
            homeBatter6 , homeBatter7 , homeBatter8 , homeBatter9
          ]) THEN homeTeamId
      WHEN pitcherId IN UNNEST([
            awayFielder1, awayFielder2, awayFielder3, awayFielder4, awayFielder5, awayFielder6,
            awayFielder7, awayFielder8, awayFielder9, awayFielder10, awayFielder11, awayFielder12,
            awayBatter1 , awayBatter2 , awayBatter3 , awayBatter4 , awayBatter5 ,
            awayBatter6 , awayBatter7 , awayBatter8 , awayBatter9
          ]) THEN awayTeamId
    END AS teamId
  FROM (
    SELECT * FROM `bigquery-public-data.baseball.games_wide`
    UNION ALL
    SELECT * FROM `bigquery-public-data.baseball.games_post_wide`
  )
  WHERE pitchSpeed > 0
)
GROUP BY teamId, pitcherId
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- Description: 9) For each team, keep only the single pitcher that owns the **overall** highest pitch speed
WITH per_pitcher AS (
  SELECT
    teamId,
    pitcherId,
    MAX(pitchSpeed) AS max_pitch_speed
  FROM (
    SELECT
      pitchSpeed,
      pitcherId,
      CASE
        WHEN pitcherId IN UNNEST([
              homeFielder1, homeFielder2, homeFielder3, homeFielder4, homeFielder5, homeFielder6,
              homeFielder7, homeFielder8, homeFielder9, homeFielder10, homeFielder11, homeFielder12,
              homeBatter1 , homeBatter2 , homeBatter3 , homeBatter4 , homeBatter5 ,
              homeBatter6 , homeBatter7 , homeBatter8 , homeBatter9
            ]) THEN homeTeamId
        WHEN pitcherId IN UNNEST([
              awayFielder1, awayFielder2, awayFielder3, awayFielder4, awayFielder5, awayFielder6,
              awayFielder7, awayFielder8, awayFielder9, awayFielder10, awayFielder11, awayFielder12,
              awayBatter1 , awayBatter2 , awayBatter3 , awayBatter4 , awayBatter5 ,
              awayBatter6 , awayBatter7 , awayBatter8 , awayBatter9
            ]) THEN awayTeamId
      END AS teamId
    FROM (
      SELECT * FROM `bigquery-public-data.baseball.games_wide`
      UNION ALL
      SELECT * FROM `bigquery-public-data.baseball.games_post_wide`
    )
    WHERE pitchSpeed > 0
  )
  GROUP BY teamId, pitcherId
)
SELECT *
FROM (
  SELECT
    teamId,
    pitcherId,
    max_pitch_speed,
    ROW_NUMBER() OVER (PARTITION BY teamId ORDER BY max_pitch_speed DESC) AS rn
  FROM per_pitcher
)
WHERE rn = 1
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- Description: 10) FINAL ANSWER – highest (non‑zero) pitch speed achieved for each team,
-- together with the pitcher’s full name
WITH unioned AS (
  SELECT
    gameId,
    pitchSpeed,
    pitcherId,
    CONCAT(pitcherFirstName, ' ', pitcherLastName) AS pitcher_name,
    -- Determine which team (home or away) the pitcher belonged to in this game
    CASE
      WHEN pitcherId IN UNNEST([
            homeFielder1, homeFielder2, homeFielder3, homeFielder4, homeFielder5, homeFielder6,
            homeFielder7, homeFielder8, homeFielder9, homeFielder10, homeFielder11, homeFielder12,
            homeBatter1 , homeBatter2 , homeBatter3 , homeBatter4 , homeBatter5 ,
            homeBatter6 , homeBatter7 , homeBatter8 , homeBatter9
          ]) THEN homeTeamId
      WHEN pitcherId IN UNNEST([
            awayFielder1, awayFielder2, awayFielder3, awayFielder4, awayFielder5, awayFielder6,
            awayFielder7, awayFielder8, awayFielder9, awayFielder10, awayFielder11, awayFielder12,
            awayBatter1 , awayBatter2 , awayBatter3 , awayBatter4 , awayBatter5 ,
            awayBatter6 , awayBatter7 , awayBatter8 , awayBatter9
          ]) THEN awayTeamId
    END AS teamId
  FROM (
    SELECT * FROM `bigquery-public-data.baseball.games_wide`
    UNION ALL
    SELECT * FROM `bigquery-public-data.baseball.games_post_wide`
  )
  WHERE pitchSpeed > 0
),
per_pitcher_team AS (
  SELECT
    teamId,
    pitcherId,
    pitcher_name,
    MAX(pitchSpeed) AS max_pitch_speed
  FROM unioned
  WHERE teamId IS NOT NULL      -- keep only rows where the ownership check succeeded
  GROUP BY teamId, pitcherId, pitcher_name
),
team_max AS (
  SELECT
    teamId,
    FIRST_VALUE(pitcherId)     OVER w AS pitcherId,
    FIRST_VALUE(pitcher_name)  OVER w AS pitcher_name,
    MAX(max_pitch_speed)       OVER w AS max_pitch_speed
  FROM per_pitcher_team
  WINDOW w AS (PARTITION BY teamId ORDER BY max_pitch_speed DESC)
)
SELECT DISTINCT teamId,
       pitcherId,
       pitcher_name,
       max_pitch_speed
FROM team_max
ORDER BY max_pitch_speed DESC    -- fastest arms first, optional
LIMIT 20;
```

Each query is limited to 20 rows so that you can run them quickly while validating every intermediate step, ending with the consolidated list of “hardest thrower per team” that merges both regular‑season and post‑season data.
